We need to produce a plan that dispatches origin_availability_alpha, destination_availability_alpha, shift_candidate_alpha, shift_candidate_beta.

We need to understand domain and planning. We have actions for dispatch: execute_origin_dispatch, execute_destination_dispatch, execute_schedule_dispatch.

The preconditions: for execute_origin_dispatch (?origin_availability - origin_candidate_availability ?vehicle_unit - vehicle_unit ?dispatch_slot - dispatch_slot):
  (and
    (dispatch_allocated ?origin_availability)
    (candidate_vehicle_linked ?origin_availability ?vehicle_unit)
    (candidate_dispatch_slot_linked ?origin_availability ?dispatch_slot)
    (not (dispatched ?origin_availability))
  )
Effect: (dispatched ?origin_availability) (vehicle_available ?vehicle_unit) (dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot)

So to dispatch an origin availability, we need dispatch_allocated, candidate_vehicle_linked, candidate_dispatch_slot_linked.

Similarly for destination: execute_destination_dispatch.

For schedule_candidate (shift candidate): execute_schedule_dispatch.

We need to allocate dispatch slots and link vehicle etc.

We have actions to allocate dispatch slot for candidate: allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate parameters (?candidate - candidate_entity ?dispatch_slot - dispatch_slot ?route_task_profile - route_task_profile)
Preconditions: (dispatch_ready ?candidate) (candidate_task_profile_linked ?candidate ?route_task_profile) (dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot) (not (dispatch_allocated ?candidate))

Effect: (dispatch_allocated ?candidate) (candidate_dispatch_slot_linked ?candidate ?dispatch_slot) (not (dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot))

Thus we need dispatch_ready and candidate_task_profile_linked.

We also need candidate_vehicle_linked, which can be done via allocate_vehicle_unit action: parameters (?candidate - candidate_entity ?vehicle_unit - vehicle_unit)
Preconditions: (candidate_created ?candidate) (not (vehicle_allocated ?candidate)) (vehicle_available ?vehicle_unit)
Effect: (vehicle_allocated ?candidate) (candidate_vehicle_linked ?candidate ?vehicle_unit) (not (vehicle_available ?vehicle_unit))

We need candidate_created (create_candidate). Also candidate_prepared (confirm_candidate_preparedness) after vehicle allocated and task profile linked.

Also candidate_task_profile_linked via attach_task_profile: parameters (?candidate - candidate_entity ?route_task_profile - route_task_profile)
Preconditions: (candidate_created ?candidate) (vehicle_allocated ?candidate) (route_task_profile_available ?route_task_profile)
Effect: (candidate_task_profile_linked ?candidate ?route_task_profile) (not (route_task_profile_available ?route_task_profile))

