Similarly for destination: we need destination_availability_locked and destination_availability_confirmed for mark_destination_availability_dispatch_ready. We can load destination payload then unload to get confirmed.

But we also need to assemble transport leg and authorize loading.

Transport leg assembly actions: there are several assemble_* actions depending on loading states. For mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready we need transport_leg_assembled and transport_leg_loading_authorized. So we need to assemble a transport leg (any of the assemble actions) and then authorize loading.

Assemble actions require origin_availability_locked and destination_availability_locked, plus node conditions (ready/occupied) etc. For basic assemble_transport_leg: requires origin_availability_locked, destination_availability_locked, origin_availability_node_linked, destination_availability_node_linked, origin_node_ready, destination_node_ready, origin_availability_confirmed, destination_availability_confirmed, transport_leg_available. Effect: transport_leg_assembled, origin linked, destination linked, not transport_leg_available.

